Millions of people around the world come to our platform to find creative ideas, dream about new possibilities and plan for memories that will last a lifetime. At Pinterest, we’re on a mission to bring everyone the inspiration to create a life they love, and that starts with the people behind the product.

Discover a career where you ignite innovation for millions, transform passion into growth opportunities, celebrate each other’s unique experiences and embrace the&nbsp; flexibility to do your best work. Creating a career you love? It’s Possible.

At Pinterest, AI isn't just a feature, it's a powerful partner that augments our creativity and amplifies our impact, and we’re looking for candidates who are excited to be a part of that. To get a complete picture of your experience and abilities, we’ll explore your foundational skills and how you collaborate with AI.

Through our interview process, what matters most is that you can always explain your approach, showing us not just what you know, but how you think. You can read more about our AI interview philosophy and how we use AI in our recruiting process here .

We’re looking for an experienced and practical lawyer to join our team supporting our Global Content Organization (GCO). This is a unique&nbsp; opportunity to join a nimble team in a growing organization and work on challenging issues in an exciting, fast-paced environment.

What you’ll do:

• Serve as the lead lawyer responsible for being the primary lawyer to the GCO organization.&nbsp;

• Draft, review, and negotiate a broad range of agreements, including creator/talent, content licensing, development, production, services, sponsorship, collaboration, co-marketing, releases, and media-buying agreements.&nbsp;

• Counsel on topics customarily supported by marketing and content lawyers, such as intellectual property rights, the FTC’s endorsement guides, rights of publicity, licensing, and promotions (e.g., contests and sweepstakes).

• Provide day-to-day legal counseling and strategic advice to GCO on creator, content, marketing, and monetization initiatives.&nbsp;

• Provide cross-functional leaders with pragmatic and strategic advice to minimize legal risks while advancing business goals and initiatives.

• Partner with cross-functional stakeholders to identify risk, propose practical paths forward, and escalate or involve subject-matter experts where appropriate.&nbsp;

• Responsibly leverage AI tools to create templates, playbooks, processes, and other solutions that improve efficiency.

• Responsibly leverage AI tools to create templates, playbooks, processes, and other solutions that improve efficiency.

What we’re looking for:

• JD with at least 10 years of experience, with substantial experience negotiating content, media, marketing, IP-adjacent, or commercial agreements, including at least 5 years in-house. Admission to a state bar with an active license in good standing is required

• Experience counseling creative, content, creator, media, marketing, or business teams at a technology, media, entertainment, advertising, or consumer-facing company. Experience at a company that operates a UGC platform is preferred.&nbsp;

• Working knowledge of intellectual property, rights clearance, right of publicity, endorsements/FTC, promotions, and related consumer-protection issues&nbsp;

• Experience with developing creative business-oriented solutions in a fast-paced environment and under tight deadlines

• Strong client-service mindset with the ability to identify, prioritize, and resolve issues independently&nbsp;

• Excellent judgment, communication skills, and a collaborative, low-ego working style&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Exceptional judgment and impeccable integrity with excellent communication skills

• Experience supporting global or multi-market initiatives is a plus&nbsp;

